      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Let me make some practical suggestions instead of emotion-first complain:\n\nI think the appropriate flow is instead of striking ban hammers to users without prior warning, should implementing a \"quarantine\" flag (soft takedown) for non appropriate contents, temporary prevents other users from accessing them (except for the moderation team), along side with notes on what element is violating which rules and correction suggestions.\n\nThis flag is different from \"non public\" as the later one third parties can still accessed via links, and will persists until the creator fixes the issue and get approved after they asks for review/appeal.\n\nAdditionally, I would also suggests temporary restrictions on uploading other contents if there are any contents under quarantine, which can prevents malicious actors doing something really harmful, or bypassing the qurantine.\n\nAgain I feels how unhealthy to the community if the red line is unclear, especially it seems not aligned to the PRs from officials, mentioning the promises to protecting both user contents and safety.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
