      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{679449d7a6c494e8ee5c9630|full_name} [Creator Guidelines](https://hello.vrchat.com/creator-guidelines) and [Community Guidelines](https://hello.vrchat.com/community-guidelines), it's not that hard man.\n\nI'm just being pedantic, but if you didn't agree with removing the world (without notice), you wouldn't be on VRChat right now. You've agreed to it in Terms of Service § 8.7 without notice. It's another thing to dislike removing the worlds and banning the creator.\n\nAnd VRChat does email you with the ban reason. The appeals are handled at https://vrch.at/moderation, you can appeal the decision.\n\nThe tags are used for filtering content users may not want to see, based on their preferences in settings. As noted in Creator Guidelines, \"[t]he presence of these content warnings does not permit you to upload content that otherwise violates the Creator Guidelines or Terms of Service.\"",
